QUESTION: Write a program to demonstrate Dictionary & related functions in python 


ALGORITHM
Algorithm
1.Start
2.Create an empty dictionary
3.Add employee names and phone numbers
4.Display dictionary
5.Add a new element
6.Update an existing value
7.Delete an element
8.Display keys, values, and items
9.Use get() to access specific value
10.Traverse dictionary using loops
11.Apply condition (check numbers starting with 9)
12.Stop


CODE 
# Creating dictionary
employee_ph = {}

employee_ph["Siya"] = "9875214556"
employee_ph["Manish"] = "9875746556"
employee_ph["Shekhar"] = "9632514876"
employee_ph["Jessica"] = "9238722524"

print("Initial Dictionary:")
print(employee_ph)

Adding element

employee_ph["Nayana"] = "8975245637"
print("\nAfter Adding Nayana:")
print(employee_ph)

Updating element

employee_ph["Shekhar"] = "8569175246"
print("\nAfter Updating Shekhar:")
print(employee_ph)

 Deleting element

del employee_ph["Jessica"]
print("\nAfter Deleting Jessica:")
print(employee_ph)

 Printing values

print("\nValues:")
print(employee_ph.values())

 Using get()

print("\nPhone number of Manish:")
print(employee_ph.get("Manish"))

 Printing keys

print("\nKeys:")
print(employee_ph.keys())

 Printing items

print("\nItems:")
print(employee_ph.items())

 Loop through keys

print("\nEmployee Names:")
for key in employee_ph:
    print(key)

 Loop through values

print("\nPhone Numbers:")
for value in employee_ph.values():
    print(value)

 Keys and values together

print("\nEmployee Details:")
for key, value in employee_ph.items():
    print("Name:", key, "| Phone:", value)

 Condition check

print("\nNumbers starting with 9:")
for key, value in employee_ph.items():
    if value.startswith("9"):
        print(key, ":", value)



